+# third_party/darkstr — Approach B FFI (patch 0008)
+
+Vendored, flattened `duppel-persona` + `duppel-ffi` for LibreWolf / Firefox **155.0.1-1**.
+
+## Why not Approach A (gkrust path-dep)?
+
+Path-dep into `toolkit/library/rust/shared` requires a live `cargo update -p gkrust-shared`
+against the train `Cargo.lock`. This pin ships **Approach B** (release cdylib + chrome
+ctypes) so symbols are reachable without rewriting the Gecko lockfile. Revisit A when
+Mini `Cargo.lock` update is proven green.
+
+## Build / install
+
+```bash
+source ~/src/darkstr-gecko/DARKSTR_GECKO_ROOT.env
+# after ./mach build at least once (dist/bin exists), or pass --prefix:
+./third_party/darkstr/build-and-install-ffi.sh --prefix "$objdir/dist/bin"
+```
+
+Chrome `DarkstrFfi.sys.mjs` dlopens `libduppel_ffi` from CurProcD/GreD and calls
+`darkstr_ffi_persona_snapshot_json` / `darkstr_ffi_abi_version` / `darkstr_ffi_string_free`.
+
+Brand: darkstr — not official LibreWolf.
